1
00:00:00,018 --> 00:00:02,618
On Venus, a day lasts longer than a year!

2
00:00:02,605 --> 00:00:06,842
Tok knocks on the door: Of course you can

3
00:00:06,642 --> 00:00:07,615
come in, Tok!

4
00:00:07,602 --> 00:00:08,882
Here to watch the sunrise?

5
00:00:09,887 --> 00:00:11,047
A week goes by...

6
00:00:11,087 --> 00:00:12,087
a month goes by...

7
00:00:12,087 --> 00:00:13,247
and it's still night!

8
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:14,687
Is the clock broken?

9
00:00:14,687 --> 00:00:15,835
No, Tok!

10
00:00:15,767 --> 00:00:18,287
The problem is Venus, which spins on its

11
00:00:18,087 --> 00:00:18,927
axis very...

12
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:19,847
very slowly.

13
00:00:20,087 --> 00:00:22,407
Do you know how long one spin takes?

14
00:00:22,527 --> 00:00:24,647
Two hundred and forty-three days!

15
00:00:24,807 --> 00:00:27,247
And to go around the Sun, two hundred

16
00:00:27,047 --> 00:00:28,047
and twenty-five.

17
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:30,087
Its day is longer than its year!

18
00:00:30,427 --> 00:00:33,747
Still, from one sunrise to the next there are

19
00:00:33,547 --> 00:00:37,067
fewer days: about one hundred and seventeen, almost

20
00:00:36,867 --> 00:00:37,987
four months!

21
00:00:38,107 --> 00:00:40,867
And Tok has a brilliant idea: leave his

22
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:41,907
homework for tomorrow!

23
00:00:41,907 --> 00:00:43,338
Nice try, Tok.

24
00:00:43,371 --> 00:00:46,691
At last, almost two months later, the sun rises!

25
00:00:46,771 --> 00:00:49,451
But Tok, you're looking the wrong way!

26
00:00:49,571 --> 00:00:52,411
Here the Sun rises in the west: Venus spins

27
00:00:52,211 --> 00:00:53,051
backwards!

28
00:00:53,093 --> 00:00:55,971
Tok turns his chair and waits again.

29
00:00:56,051 --> 00:00:57,091
Now you know:
